  "changes": [
    "Corrected source-to-authored-rig rest axes for combat only; the previously airborne horns now follow the source ground sweep.",
    "Retained FIG segmented slam and sweep playback, all seven sidesweep joints and early turning windows.",
    "Exact authored cuboid contacts sampled at 1/16 tick; active windows, wall occlusion, damage vetoes and one shared victim ledger.",
    "Body scrape and articulated head/jaw ground contact each release once; three source expansion events propagate from the actual support, with actual material fragments and item impulses.",
    "Timestamped accepted-hit tissue/crush effects and spatial audio; no success feedback on a miss.",
    "Head, neck, jaw and horn cuboids participate in obstacle checks. Confirmed wall impact produces material chips and sound, without ground ripples or victim blood.",
    "Ordinary cancellation retracts the accepted pose and retires all pending hit, ground and wave events."
  ],
  "regressionNotes": [
    "The older autonomous Hydra test expected damage at the rooted owner radius. It now places the target in the visible slam reach and verifies autonomous choice, windup, one accepted blow and recovery.",
    "Hydra GameTests use a 32-block arena to keep their enlarged reach out of adjacent encounter fixtures.",
    "Gecko diagnostic world matrices cancel the outer body-size transform; QA restores that known outer render transform, the .01 local draw lift, interpolated body yaw and six-tick entry blend before comparison."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Source joints, curves and FIG fields are verified; exact original transition conditions, target strategy, procedural controllers and sound patch waveforms remain incomplete.",
    "Fixed-length block-model retargeting, cuboid collision, source damage ratios against the MC attack attribute, and support-based waves are explicit MC adaptations.",
    "Obstacle rewind, two-tick visual prediction and at most 0.6 radians of backwards rest bending are MC adaptations, not recovered original procedural controllers. Enclosed obstacles that cannot be cleared by this bounded bend still require a broader solver.",
    "Terrain displacement is visual with physical loose-item response, not persistent excavation or world block deformation.",
    "Hidden muted QA verifies cue scheduling and resources, not subjective listening or original audio identity.",
    "Incoming multipart hit detection, original victim reaction clips, player absorb combinations and other creatures still need the full-goal review. No release package is asserted by this report."
  ],
